  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Project commissioned by Thyssen-Bornemisza Art Contemporary, Vienna, on invitation by the 51st Biennale di Venezia, as a part of the exhibition, Always a little further, curated by Rosa Martinez"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">" ... centers on an astronomical spectacle: every year the Perseids can be seen in the first half of August as a shower of falling stars whose name has its origins in the constellation "Perseus". In reference to the martyrdom of St. Lawrence on August 10, AD 258 the Perseid meteors are often referred to as the "Tears of St. Lawrence". The work is presented to would-be observers who can locate viewing times for "Tears of St. Lawrence" by consulting the timetable in this booklet. The book also provides historical and scientific background information on the meteor shower as well as a glossary of terms and a post card for the reader to mail his or her observations to the International Meteor Organization."--Printed Matter catalog.</subfield>
  </datafield>
